#: ../../technical/articles/009-cl-ve-permanente-browser-support-and-sede-read-primitives.md:12
msgid ""
"This chunk covers 29 files (5,413 assigned lines; 46,507 measured proxy "
"tokens) across AEAT Cl@ve Permanente authentication, encrypted browser-"
"session persistence, Playwright browser construction and health checks, "
"Sede shared helpers, and declarations-listing and artefact-fetch "
"primitives. All nine bounded pages were read in full, including the "
"explicit slices. This is static analysis of the repository snapshot: I "
"did not launch a browser, contact AEAT, run the application, or verify "
"the current behavior of external sites. Comments that describe "
"measurements or live captures are attributed to the code, not "
"independently validated here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/009-cl-ve-permanente-browser-support-and-sede-read-primitives.md:14
msgid "Capabilities and operation"
msgstr "Capacidades y funcionamiento"

#: ../../technical/articles/009-cl-ve-permanente-browser-support-and-sede-read-primitives.md:16
msgid ""
"The auth provider offers a headless DNI/NIE-and-password route for Cl@ve "
"Permanente, intended for supported Sede read paths. It classifies the "
"configured identity, enforces remote-operation policies for username and "
"password entry and the submit click, parses a closed set of IdP errors, "
"and treats an SMS elevation prompt as unsupported rather than trying to "
"bypass it. Authentication captures browser storage state and returns a "
"provider-specific session; subsequent verification requires the exact "
"active session object and probes an AEAT landing. The code therefore "
"separates a successful form submission from the later session assertion, "
"although the fresh-login gate is weaker than that later verifier, "
"described below (clave_permanente.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/clave_permanente.py`), "
"clave_permanente.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/clave_permanente.py`), "
"clave_permanente.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/clave_permanente.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/009-cl-ve-permanente-browser-support-and-sede-read-primitives.md:18
msgid ""
"The shared session store adapts persisted browser state to the secure-"
"object repository under the AEAT browser-session namespace. It validates "
"the JSON-shaped state and metadata, timestamps writes, computes a "
"canonical storage-state digest, and validates the stored data on load. "
"`DeferredSessionWrites` stages save/delete operations in a context-local "
"buffer and only publishes them when explicitly committed; leaving the "
"context without publish discards staged operations. The adapter also "
"refuses a legacy product-specific session path instead of adopting or "
"migrating prior state. Auth metadata permits a missing landing URL, and "
"the shared Sede bridge loads decrypted storage state into a `dict` for "
"context creation (session_store.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/session_store.py`), "
"session_store.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/session_store.py`), "
"session_store.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/session_store.py`), "
"session_store.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/session_store.py`), "
"clave_permanente_metadata.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/clave_permanente_metadata.py`),"
" _auth_state.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_auth_state.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/009-cl-ve-permanente-browser-support-and-sede-read-primitives.md:20
msgid ""
"Browser factories own the Playwright runtime and browser lifetime, apply "
"the configured evasion strategy before returning contexts, and make "
"teardown failures observable through typed errors/logging. Context setup "
"includes profile locale/timezone, saved state or an injected certificate "
"provisioner, and `accept_downloads=False`. `BrowserSession.navigate` adds"
" response classification for network failures, maintenance banners, WAF "
"challenges, and rate limiting. Its parser uses evidence thresholds "
"instead of a single phrase: maintenance is accepted from multiple body "
"markers or a body/title combination, WAF detection requires status/marker"
" combinations, and rate-limit responses can interpret integer or HTTP-"
"date `Retry-After` values. When multiple conditions fit, maintenance on "
"503 is considered before generic rate limiting. A standalone connectivity"
" probe creates a browser/session and returns the corresponding health "
"status or a typed failure (factory.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/factory.py`), factory.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/factory.py`), session.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/session.py`), session.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/session.py`), "
"_site_health_parsers.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/_site_health_parsers.py`), "
"_site_health_parsers.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/_site_health_parsers.py`), "
"_site_health_parsers.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/_site_health_parsers.py`), "
"_site_health_parsers.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/_site_health_parsers.py`), "
"connectivity.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/connectivity.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/009-cl-ve-permanente-browser-support-and-sede-read-primitives.md:22
msgid ""
"The Sede helpers consolidate authorization checks for browser actions and"
" HTTP reads, element lookup, response normalization, redacted URL "
"projection, and negative-first identity verdict parsing. Their central "
"`assert_read_landing` rule validates the actual landed URL against the "
"surface policy and a per-surface path-prefix allow-list. Its purpose is "
"important because a browser click can dispatch a form POST that neither a"
" source-level forbidden-verb scan nor a request guard sees. The "
"declarations fetch layer uses this when a popup opens a justificante, "
"extracts a CSV identifier only after the popup lands on the cotejo path, "
"constructs a PDF URL from the observed origin, validates its read guard, "
"then requires a 2xx response, non-empty body, and exact `application/pdf`"
" media type. Submitted-file capture expects a browser download event, "
"cancels it best-effort, and re-fetches the download URL through the "
"authenticated in-memory request context; it records hash, byte count, "
"source URL, and capture time rather than persisting the downloaded bytes "
"to disk. The ZK listbox parser converts visible rows into typed "
"declarations, obtains the total from the pager when available, identifies"
" action columns by normalized headers, rejects missing justificante "
"headers, and preserves whether the displayed page may be truncated "
"(_adapter_utils.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_adapter_utils.py`), "
"_adapter_utils.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_adapter_utils.py`), "
"_adapter_utils.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_adapter_utils.py`), "
"_adapter_utils.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_adapter_utils.py`), "
"_declarations_fetch.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_declarations_fetch.py`), "
"_declarations_fetch.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_declarations_fetch.py`), "
"_declarations_fetch.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_declarations_fetch.py`), "
"_declarations_listbox.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_declarations_listbox.py`), "
"_declarations_listbox.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_declarations_listbox.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/009-cl-ve-permanente-browser-support-and-sede-read-primitives.md:24
msgid ""
"Other small modules support the same flow: shape diagnostics reduce a "
"page to bounded labels/counts and a content hash; browser-stage wrappers "
"translate Playwright timeout and general errors into stable Sede error "
"categories; `operator_progress` emits only while a context-local sink is "
"installed; the registry renderer maps typed records to fixed-width bytes "
"but the export package declares live writes out of scope. These are "
"supporting interfaces, not a complete user-facing export or filing "
"workflow (_declarations_diagnostics.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_declarations_diagnostics.py`),"
" _browser_stage.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_browser_stage.py`), "
"operator_progress.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/operator_progress.py`), "
"registry_record_renderer.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/export/registry_record_renderer.py`),"
" export/__init__.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/export/__init__.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/009-cl-ve-permanente-browser-support-and-sede-read-primitives.md:26
msgid "Data, security, and assessment"
msgstr "Datos, seguridad y evaluación"

#: ../../technical/articles/009-cl-ve-permanente-browser-support-and-sede-read-primitives.md:28
msgid ""
"Credentials and browser state cross distinct trust boundaries. Cl@ve "
"credentials are unwrapped only for the form operation; the remote guard "
"limits the permitted IdP/AEAT origins and action labels. Session state is"
" passed through the secure-object adapter and compared using a canonical "
"digest on resume. Certificate bytes are not part of this provider, but "
"provider selection exposes a certificate context provisioner for AEAT-"
"origin contexts. The browser context explicitly disables Chromium "
"download persistence, while the declarations capture path reuses the "
"authenticated request context for bytes. Site-health records retain "
"bounded evidence fragments; Sede diagnostics remove URL query and "
"fragment, cap displayed text, and avoid embedding full row-cell values in"
" malformed-row errors (clave_permanente_support.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/clave_permanente_support.py`), "
"provider_selection.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/provider_selection.py`), "
"session.py (`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/session.py`), "
"site_health_records.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/site_health_records.py`), "
"_adapter_utils.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_adapter_utils.py`), "
"_declarations_listbox.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_declarations_listbox.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/009-cl-ve-permanente-browser-support-and-sede-read-primitives.md:30
msgid ""
"One concrete auth boundary deserves follow-up: fresh Cl@ve login waits "
"for a URL pattern containing the expected target path and then "
"captures/persists the browser state; it does not appear to apply the same"
" canonical AEAT host-and-path predicate used by `verify`. That means a "
"redirect on an unexpected host containing the target path could be "
"accepted as a fresh login landing before a later verification rejects it."
" This is a conditional risk, not proof of a reachable bypass; confirm the"
" exact Playwright wait semantics and all caller ordering in the "
"authenticator. The form driver also treats several page methods as "
"optional and can continue without them if the supplied page port omits "
"`fill`, `click`, or `content`; whether a real production page can satisfy"
" that shape is an adapter-contract question. Separately, the persisted "
"metadata allows `landing_url=None`, and verification then falls back to a"
" configured Sede path/probe URL, so the fallback path should be checked "
"against dispatcher behavior and whether it can initiate authentication "
"(clave_permanente.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/clave_permanente.py`), "
"clave_permanente.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/clave_permanente.py`), "
"clave_permanente.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/clave_permanente.py`), "
"clave_permanente.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/clave_permanente.py`), "
"clave_permanente.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/clave_permanente.py`), "
"clave_permanente_metadata.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/auth/clave_permanente_metadata.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/009-cl-ve-permanente-browser-support-and-sede-read-primitives.md:32
msgid ""
"The health wrapper is additive: direct `page.goto` remains legal and "
"bypasses automatic site-health classification. Its implementation also "
"logs the requested full URL and reads the full page content before "
"classification; records bound by the parser do not impose a cap on that "
"initial content allocation. These are meaningful privacy and resource "
"considerations for callers that place identifiers in query strings or "
"process very large responses. The Sede shared landing rule is stronger "
"because it reasons about the actual host and path, but its path test is a"
" prefix check. A prefix that is too broad can include sibling AEAT "
"endpoints, so each caller’s configured prefix must remain narrow. Browser"
" action/read guards and a text fixture listing forbidden write verbs are "
"useful defense-in-depth; the fixture is static data and by itself proves "
"neither scan coverage nor live no-write behavior (session.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/session.py`), "
"_site_health_parsers.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/browser/_site_health_parsers.py`), "
"_adapter_utils.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_adapter_utils.py`), "
"_no_write_surface_fixture.txt "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/outbound/aeat/sede/_no_write_surface_fixture.txt`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/009-cl-ve-permanente-browser-support-and-sede-read-primitives.md:34
msgid ""
"Parser strengths include negative markers taking precedence over positive"
" identity markers, strict PDF MIME equality, structured external-shape "
"errors, and optional pager totals that can expose incomplete listings. An"
" absent pager is treated as a complete single-page result, however, which"
" relies on AEAT markup semantics. Malformed rows with fewer than seven "
"cells are skipped; a changed shape can therefore reduce results without a"
" parse failure if the pager does not expose a total. Several parsers "
"normalize or lowercase complete HTML/text strings, so memory use is "
"proportional to the incoming document. The chunk contains no tests, and "
"comments refer to external tests or live captures that were not inspected"
" as part of this chunk. Static source alone cannot establish AEAT "
"compatibility or whether all navigation call sites use the guarded "
"helpers. Cross-layer synthesis should resolve callers of provider "
"verification, secure repository guarantees, declarations "
"orchestration/pagination, and whether the add-on navigation health probe "
"is used consistently."
msgstr ""

